{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/GettingStarted"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Unify3Sdk"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Getting Started with Unify3Sdk"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/unify3sdk\/gettingstarted"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A walkthrough of the main Unify3Sdk workflow."}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Articles","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/TestContexts","doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/PerformingCalibration","doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/Logging"],"title":"Articles"}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The main entry point is "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/Unify"},{"type":"text","text":", and most applications begin with the shared singleton:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let unify = Unify.shared"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide assumes you’re comfortable reading Swift and using Swift concurrency, but you do not need to know the SDK in advance."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Understand-the-SDKs-async-model","type":"heading","text":"Understand the SDK’s async model"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The SDK uses two async patterns:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Some APIs are one-shot ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"text":" calls that complete once, such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"connectInstrument(serialNumber:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"runBluetoothScan()"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"stopBluetoothScan()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Other APIs return async streams that keep yielding values over time, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"runInstrumentDiscovery()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"runTest(checkRl:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"getRealtimeTestResults()"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"getBatchedTestResults()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"That split is useful to keep in mind as you read the API surface: some calls perform a single action, while others represent an ongoing flow of updates.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Start with `Unify.shared`","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Start-with-Unifyshared"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Unify.shared"},{"text":" is the main interface for the SDK. You use it to discover instruments, connect to them, configure a test, run that test, and collect results.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Discover instruments","level":2,"anchor":"Discover-instruments","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IwaReturnLossFrequencyExample"},{"text":" example starts by scanning for nearby instruments and then listening for discovery updates. That is a good mental model for real applications too.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Scanning is a one-shot async action, while discovery is a stream because the visible set of instruments can change over time. A typical flow is:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"start scanning","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"consume values from "},{"code":"runInstrumentDiscovery()","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"choose an instrument from the discovered snapshot"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"connect with "},{"code":"connectInstrument(serialNumber:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Once you have chosen an instrument, you can read its definition before building a test so that your configuration matches the connected hardware.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Configure-a-test","type":"heading","text":"Configure a test"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The SDK works with one configured ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/Test","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" at a time. That test can contain one or more traces, so even a single test run may produce several outputs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You will see the same pattern in several SDK types: a single API value can carry one of a few concrete shapes. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/Trace","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is an early example. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Test.traces"},{"text":" is a list of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trace"},{"text":" values, and each entry holds one specific trace kind. Most of the time you can pass those values around uniformly, then inspect the concrete case only when you need trace-specific settings or data.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Before you start a measurement, call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"configureTest(test:)"},{"text":". This gives the SDK a chance to validate the request and return a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/TestConfigurationResult","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" that tells you whether the configuration is valid.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TestConfigurationResult"},{"text":" is also a useful place to inspect the configured traces and initial trace contexts. If you want to modify an existing configured trace, the easiest path is usually to start from the configured trace returned in that result and update it while preserving its trace identifier, rather than rebuilding the trace from scratch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Run-the-test","type":"heading","text":"Run the test"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"After configuration succeeds, start the measurement with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"runTest(checkRl:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is a stream of progress updates, not a single completion callback. In other words, you typically iterate over the values it yields until the stream finishes:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["for try await progressUpdate in unify.runTest(checkRl: true) {","    let percentage = progressUpdate.traceProgress","    print(\"Progress: \\(percentage * 100)%\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For a getting-started workflow, it is enough to think of this stream as “the test is still running and here is its latest progress.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Get-results","type":"heading","text":"Get results"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The SDK gives you two main ways to consume test results:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"getRealtimeTestResults()"},{"text":" for live updates while the test is running","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"getBatchedTestResults()"},{"type":"text","text":" for a simpler stream of complete results"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you are just getting started, the batched path is usually the easiest one to begin with, and it is the one used in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IwaReturnLossFrequencyExample"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["if let testResult = try await unify.getBatchedTestResults().first(where: { _ in true }) {","    print(\"Got \\(testResult.tracePoints.count) points.\")","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you need live visual updates or progressive processing, look at the realtime API instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Next step","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Next-step"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Once this flow makes sense, read through the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IwaReturnLossFrequencyExample"},{"text":" example from top to bottom. It shows the same sequence in a compact, working example: start from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Unify.shared"},{"text":", discover an instrument, configure a test, run it, and read the results.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://com.kaelus.unify3sdk/documentation/Unify3Sdk/Unify":{"abstract":[{"text":"The main unify interface","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Unify"}],"url":"\/documentation\/unify3sdk\/unify","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Unify"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/Unify","title":"Unify","kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.kaelus.unify3sdk/documentation/Unify3Sdk/Trace":{"url":"\/documentation\/unify3sdk\/trace","title":"Trace","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/Trace","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trace"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trace"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A trace."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://com.kaelus.unify3sdk/documentation/Unify3Sdk/Logging":{"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Logging","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure log filtering and display the log stream."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/unify3sdk\/logging","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/Logging"},"doc://com.kaelus.unify3sdk/documentation/Unify3Sdk":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Discover instruments, configure tests, run measurements, and read results from Swift.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/unify3sdk","title":"Unify3Sdk"},"doc://com.kaelus.unify3sdk/documentation/Unify3Sdk/PerformingCalibration":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/PerformingCalibration","role":"article","title":"Performing a Calibration","url":"\/documentation\/unify3sdk\/performingcalibration","abstract":[{"text":"Configure and run an OSL calibration.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://com.kaelus.unify3sdk/documentation/Unify3Sdk/TestContexts":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How to decide whether a trace is ready to run."}],"type":"topic","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/unify3sdk\/testcontexts","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/TestContexts","title":"Understanding Test Contexts","kind":"article"},"doc://com.kaelus.unify3sdk/documentation/Unify3Sdk/TestConfigurationResult":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/TestConfigurationResult","role":"symbol","title":"TestConfigurationResult","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TestConfigurationResult","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/unify3sdk\/testconfigurationresult","abstract":[{"text":"The result of configuring a test.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TestConfigurationResult"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.kaelus.unify3sdk/documentation/Unify3Sdk/Test":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"Test","abstract":[{"text":"Test is used to configure a collection of measurements.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Test","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Test","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/unify3sdk\/test","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.kaelus.unify3sdk\/documentation\/Unify3Sdk\/Test"}}}